phy (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Rep. Greg Murphy seeks another term in a northeastern North Carolina district that leans about six points Republican. He enters the final stretch with a large financial edge, roughly $2.3 million on hand to Democrat Raymond Smith Jr.'s $44,000, and a late Trump rally in Greenville bolsters Republican turnout. A group opposing Murphy has spent modestly, the only meaningful outside money in the race.\n\nThe Democratic-leaning national environment helps Smith, and an August poll from a Democratic-affiliated firm showed the contest at just three points, while prediction markets give Smith roughly a one-in-three chance of winning. Most professional raters still call the district Likely Republican, with a couple rating it Lean Republican. The balance of evidence points to a Murphy win, though with more uncertainty than a typical incumbent seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0567, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0798, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0901, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1267, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.114, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1275, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1234, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0732, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0908, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0684, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0985, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0906, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -8.0}, {